# agentflow workflow (Cursor)

This project uses a token-efficient, persistent agent workflow. The
**deterministic** parts — knowledge freshness, validation, lifecycle
transitions, closure gates, and retry/spawn limits — live in a
platform-independent core, not in prompts:

```
node .agentflow/cli.mjs <command>
```

Never duplicate that logic in chat. Always call the core and read `.agent/`.

## Roles

| Role | Owns | Read-only? |
|------|------|-----------|
| Conductor | lifecycle, delegation (this primary session) | no edits |
| Analyzer | `.agent/knowledge/` | no source edits |
| Planner | `.agent/tasks/<id>/plan.json` | plan only |
| Executor | implementation, `progress.json`, `result.json` | no knowledge/plan edits |
| Reviewer | verification findings, `discrepancies.json` | read-only |
| Consultant | recommendations | read-only |

Subagents are defined in `.cursor/agents/`. Invoke them with `/analyzer`,
`/planner`, `/executor`, `/reviewer`, `/consultant`. Full contracts:
`.agentflow/docs/agents/`. Shared rules: `.agentflow/docs/agents/README.md`.

## Conductor behaviour (default)

1. Select the active task and check knowledge readiness:
   `node .agentflow/cli.mjs status --json`.
2. Delegate to **one** role at a time. Never spawn unbounded trees; the project
   core enforces persisted spawn limits and Cursor enforces a nesting limit.
3. Enforce transitions with the core:
   `node .agentflow/cli.mjs transition --task <id> --to <status>`.
4. Verify closure before completion:
   `node .agentflow/cli.mjs close --task <id> --json`. If it fails, report
   the gate reasons; never force the transition.
5. Stop and ask the user at approval boundaries: architecture change, scope
   change, destructive/external operation, unmet acceptance criteria.

## Shared rules (all roles)

- **Read the index first.** Trust `fresh` knowledge and `approved` plans; never
  rescan the repository for something already recorded as `fresh`.
- **Artifacts are the handoff.** Chat carries a task ID, artifact `path#Heading`
  references, the next action, and blocker IDs — nothing more.
- **Independent verification.** Do not accept claims at face value; re-run the
  declared commands and record observed results. Never fabricate results.
- **Reference as `path#Heading`**, never line numbers.
- **Do not store secrets** or copy large source excerpts into artifacts.
- **Do not bypass a deterministic gate.** If blocked by something outside your
  authority, stop and report instead of guessing.

## Shell boundaries

`.cursor/hooks.json` registers a guard (`beforeShellExecution`) that denies
privilege escalation, broad recursive deletion, `git push`, destructive git
resets, publish, and download-piped-to-shell; other commands (core CLI, git
inspection, tests, read-only tools) are allowed, and installs/network/containers
require approval. Run the core via the exact path `.agentflow/cli.mjs`.
